Z||000004||Black88GT||01-23-2001||08:46 AM||||I have seen the blue distributor cap at Auto Zone, and the Fiero Store (same price, 10 bucks).  However I don't think its the same blue as the 8mm Splitfire wires that the Fiero Store sells.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Alex4mula||01-23-2001||10:59 AM||||The best blue wries you can get are the Jacobs Electronics wires (http://www.jacobselectronics.com). Cost around $65 and have a life time warranty. You will feel the difference. You can look mines at community.webtv.net/alexft/Alex4mula<BR>||||reg||1
